{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":79561,"duration_api_ms":79534,"num_turns":11,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"d8f8f411-a331-49f5-bb5f-f99e4b15765f","total_cost_usd":0.43029124999999996,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":38479,"cache_read_input_tokens":216675,"output_tokens":3257,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":38479,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":7,"outputTokens":3257,"cacheReadInputTokens":216675,"cacheCreationInputTokens":38479,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.43029124999999996,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"All four amendments identify real, verified issues in the codebase. Amendments fr-4-4e504190 and fr-4-6f70d3c3 describe the same dimensional mismatch bug from complementary angles — both are valid and should be accepted. Amendment fr-4-92b6a31f addresses the test gap that allowed the mismatch to go undetected. Amendment fr-4-0a3f3f58 identifies a real stability tracker reseeding gap in the v2→v3 migration path.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-4-4e504190","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: lines 60-61 of plant_growth.rs pass raw mg totals from total_substrate_n()/total_substrate_p() (which sum layer.nutrient_store_mg_n_total) against half-saturation constants that have been divided by 20 via legacy_total_param_to_mg_per_l(). This is a clear dimensional mismatch — e.g. half_saturation(40, 0.4) ≈ 0.99 — making substrate limitation effectively non-functional. The water column path (lines 52-58) correctly uses mg/L for both arguments. The amendment correctly identifies the fix options: either normalize substrate totals to a density/concentration or use the original total-based constants for the substrate path."},{"amendment_id":"fr-4-92b6a31f","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: the existing test plant_water_column_limitation_is_volume_invariant_at_fixed_concentration sets substrate_uptake_bias to 0.0 and clears substrate_layers, completely bypassing the substrate limitation code path. A test with nonzero substrate bias and varying substrate nutrient levels is needed to cover the substrate half-saturation path. This is a genuine test coverage gap that allowed the dimensional mismatch to persist."},{"amendment_id":"fr-4-0a3f3f58","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: migrate_schema_v2_to_v3() (save.rs:76-82) only calls rescale_totals_for_volume on water state but never reseeds stability_tracker. The stability_tracker field uses #[serde(default)] (state.rs:47), so v2 saves missing this field get defaults (temp=25, pH=7, gh=7, do=6). enforce_invariants() only clamps instability_index — it does not reseed prev_* baselines. Meanwhile, TankState::new() and TankState::with_geometry() both properly call seed_from_water after construction/rescaling. The migration path is the only code path that rescales water totals without reseeding the tracker, creating a real risk of bogus instability spikes on first daily update after loading a v2 save."},{"amendment_id":"fr-4-6f70d3c3","decision":"accept","rationale":"This describes the same core bug as fr-4-4e504190 but adds the important observation about volume/footprint invariance: because substrate limitation uses absolute mg totals, a tank with twice the substrate mass will appear twice as nutrient-rich to plants regardless of tank geometry, breaking the invariance that the water column path achieves via concentration-based units. Both the dimensional mismatch fix and the invariance concern are valid and worth addressing together."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"2d5becbe-94a7-45bb-b58f-f1f93205431b"}
